This dataset is from the paper "Representational Similarity Analysis of the Neural Representations of Orthographic, Phonological, Semantic, and Intermediate Mappings During Single Word Reading". Fifty participants underwent MRI scanning and behavioural tests. In the behavioural session participants performed the Phonemic Decoding Efficiency and Sight Word Efficiency subtests of the TWRE, Block Design and Matrix Reasoning from WASI-II, Rapid Automatized Naming for letters and colours, Passage Comprehension from WJ-III, and a 464-word naming task to extract sensitivity to orthographic-phonological regularities and sensitivity to orthographic-semantic effects. In the neuroimaging session, participants underwent T1w scan, fMRI scanning, and DWI (not included). Raw data are provided here.
